omxplorer, a desktop spreadsheet app (1440x900), on its Report tab over sales-1m (1,000,000 rows). The same slim menu bar on top, then a floating toolbar island: "Tiles of" with a column dropdown "amount", then buttons Sum tile, Average tile, Median tile, Distinct tile, Count tile, Chart tile, then "Filter · every tile" with a dropdown "region = South", and on the right Format, Open. The report page: title "Report" with a caption "sales-1m · region = South · 1,000,000 rows · 4 ms on the GPU". A tidy grid of equal tiles, three per row: "Sum of amount 920,404,385.00", "Median of amount 5,008.11", "Average of amount 5,004.92", "Distinct of region 5", "Count of order 199,812", each with a small "region = South" chip; one tile hovered shows a small ✕ inside its top-right corner. Then a wide chart tile "amount by region" (bars). Bottom strip: tabs "Sheet" "Report" (active) "+", and "Filtered: 199,812 of 1,000,000 rows · RTX 4090".
